<title>GERMANY: EU cattle population at 84.1 million in Dec count.</title>
<headline>EU cattle population at 84.1 million in Dec count.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cattle numbers in the European Union at the last count in December 1996 were only slightly down from a year earlier at 84.1 million, the Bonn farm ministry said in a weekly circular on Monday.</p>
<p>The figure, which applied to both cows and bulls, was down by 665,000 from December 1995.</p>
<p>France had 20.6 million animals and Germany 15.7 million.</p>
<p>Falls were registered in Germany, Britain, France, the Netherlands and Belgium while Spain and Ireland increased their cattle numbers.</p>
<p>Included in the total were 22.1 million dairy cows, of which Germany had the highest share at 5.2 million.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
